"id": "stratagraft",
"hook": "Lab-grown living skin for deep burns 🔥",
"fact": "StrataGraft is a sheet of living human skin cells grown in a lab on a mouse collagen base and placed on surgically prepared deep partial-thickness burns. Its cells release growth factors that support healing and are gradually replaced by the patient's own cells, which can reduce how much healthy skin has to be harvested for grafting. The FDA approved it in 2021, and because mouse cells were used early in its development, the FDA classifies it as a xenotransplantation product.",
